</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Wube Haile Maryam was the lord of Semien who also ruled Tigray from 1831 to 1855, making him one of the strongest regional rulers of the Ethiopian Era of Princes.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/wuchang"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/wuchang.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Wuchang</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Wuchang is a historic city on the Yangtze River in central China, now part of the city of Wuhan.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/wuchang-uprising"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/wuchang-uprising.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Wuchang Uprising</span><span class="enc-type">Revolt · 1911</span><span class="enc-snip">The Wuchang Uprising was an army mutiny in the city of Wuchang, now part of Wuhan, on 10 October 1911.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/wuffa"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/wuffa.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Wuffa</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Wuffa was the semi-legendary founder of the East Anglian royal house, from whom the dynasty took the name Wuffingas.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/wuffingas"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/wuffingas.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Wuffingas</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Wuffingas were the ruling dynasty of the Anglo-Saxon kingdom of East Anglia from the 6th century until about 749, named after their ancestor Wuffa.</span></a></li></ul>
